What is copy-on-write (COW)

	using fork() when a new process is created that is called child process from which process it is created it is called parent process.

	A variable that is common to both the parent and child processes is stored in a memory location known to both. As long as both processes only read this shared data, there is no problem. However, if either the parent or the child process modifies the shared data, the operating system creates a separate copy of that memory page for the modifying process. This mechanism is known as copy-on-write.


	refer p13.c

	
What is orphan process ?

	In parent and child process relation if parent process terminated first than child process is called orphan process. 

	for all orphan process init (pid : 1) will act as parent 

	refer p14.c


What is Zombie process ?

	In parent and child prcoess relation if child process terminated first, but parent process not terminated (not collected the status of the child) then child becomes Zombie process. 

	The resource is not released. 
		
	refer p15.c
	
	Creating Zombie process resource shortge will occur. 

	To avoid this parent need to collect the status of the child. 

	refer 16.c 

	
















































